# A list held in a record and pushed onto, with the loop's end written as an
# `if`: `if (k == 0) b (fill (bag (push b.items k) …) (k - 1))`. kanso#1926
# grows such a field in place when every mention of the record is a field
# read, and #2106 let the early answer of a `return b if` guard off that rule
# because it runs instead of the push. The `if` arm that answers `b` runs
# instead of the push too, but it still counted, so every lap copied the list
# on both engines: 80,000 pushes took 14 seconds natively and 30 on the
# interpreter, where the guard's spelling took a tenth of a second.
type bag
  items
  n

fn fill b k
  if (k == 0) b (fill (bag (push b.items k) (b.n + 1)) (k - 1))

pub fn total k
  length (fill (bag [] 0) k).items
